# SRW3 Phase 1H — in-process shadow hook for Geth v1.17.7
#
# STATUS: NOT BUILT (disclosed).  This sandbox has no Go toolchain; the
# reproducible Phase 1H experiment intentionally runs the OFFICIAL prebuilt
# client binary UNMODIFIED (client/CLIENT-SELECTION.md).  This patch is the
# SPECIFIED in-process variant of the same gate: it inserts a non-blocking
# shadow observation at the exact source-level insertion point identified in
# client/INSERTION-POINT.md (end of ConsensusAPI.newPayload, after
# InsertBlockWithoutSetHead has succeeded and before the VALID status is
# returned).  It NEVER changes the returned PayloadStatusV1 (shadow mode;
# phase spec sections 3/6/15).
#
# To build (in an environment with Go >= 1.27):
#   git clone --depth 1 --branch v1.17.7 https://github.com/ethereum/go-ethereum
#   cd go-ethereum && git apply srw3-shadow-hook.patch
#   make geth
# The hook writes one JSON line per executed payload to SRW3_SHADOW_SOCK
# (unix datagram, fire-and-forget) or, if unset, does nothing.  The SRW3
# sidecar (phase1h/python/) evaluates the gate; a future consensus-visible
# variant would additionally require the protocol change documented in the
# Phase 1H report section 27 (it can NOT be done client-locally).
diff --git a/eth/catalyst/api.go b/eth/catalyst/api.go
index 0000000..0000001 100644
--- a/eth/catalyst/api.go
+++ b/eth/catalyst/api.go
@@ -1041,6 +1041,11 @@ func (api *ConsensusAPI) newPayload(ctx context.Context, params engine.Executabl
 		ProcessingTime: processingTime,
 	})
 
+	// SRW3 shadow gate (Phase 1H): observe the executed payload.  This is
